<h4 class="boldbyline">
Re: Waterboarded
</h4>

<p>
Man, I don't know what to think about this. In a way, I think it is a good, brave thing -- the only way to get a feel for what prisoners go through. But... hmmm... I don't know. <br />
I think we all try to do what we can to channel our characters and to feel what they went through. We go down to the pit where a near-dead woman was dumped and claw our way up, as she did in the middle of the night, dirt cascading, to see how strong and scared she  must have been to do it, how much she wanted to survive. We go through the forest where people were lost and sit quiet at murder scenes. We listen to the dead's favorite songs and go to their favorite places. <br />
How is this waterboarding thing different? <br />
<br />
P.S. The word I'm being asked to type below is "horrors." Fitting. <br />

</p>
