                            <a name="comment2824"></a>
<h4 class="boldbyline">
Re: Waterboarded
</h4>

<p>
Again, not the same as torture, but one of our reporters got "arrested" and then wrote about it. Since we write so often about people who actually get arrested, it might have some benefit to know what it's actually like.<br />
<br />
As for the waterboarding, I'm still not sure what benefit it gives. On the one hand it would be an interesting and scary first-person account of how it feels but on the other, does it help with understanding the issue. We are after all talking about torture, everyone realizes it is an unpleasant experience, to put it lightly.
</p>
